  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nIn-place translation provided by browsers is extremely useful feature. Sadly the translation service often butchers names of people and companies/products.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nThere is a translate=\"no\" attribute, but using this for part of the sentence results the sentence split into multiple parts with unusable translation.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nI propose adding a translate=\"name\" (or similar) extension that can hint to the translation engine that this part of the text is a name which translation can be then handled properly. For example:\n```html\n<div><span translate=\"name\">Rene</span> bought an <span translate=\"name\">Apple</span>.</div>\n```\n",
